// Lesson 8.5 — Boss Playtest with Friends & Win/Lose Loop
// Level 3 (Outline Only): wire the real win condition (reward drop / portal / Victory UI)
// and confirm StatManager.Die() loss reset cleanly, PLUS run blind Friend Playtests where
// friends play without verbal hints so you catch real confusion before final revisions.
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';
import { renderAskBanner } from '../../lib/walkthrough';
import { renderDecompose } from '../../lib/decompose';

const DECOMPOSE = {
  big: 'Make both winning and losing real, then have friends playtest your boss blind and log every surprise.',
  parts: [
    {
      name: 'Wire the victory payoff on boss defeat and verify StatManager.Die() reset',
      doc: '5.3 (`StatManager.Die()` resetting health, halving coins, and calling `LoadScene(current.name)`)',
      href: '5.3.html',
    },
    {
      name: 'Run a hands-off friend playtest and separate confusion, bugs, and balance notes',
      doc: '7.7 / Playtest protocol below (silent observation + top-3 triage)',
      href: '7.7.html',
    },
  ],
  why:
    'You already know how to beat your own boss because you wrote the timers and placed every platform. Your friends do not. Watching two classmates play silently without you explaining a single rule exposes unclear doors, hidden hitboxes, and soft-locks faster than another hour of solo tweaking.',
  turns: [
    'When the boss dies (`health <= 0`), why should victory drop an interactive goal (`itemDrop`, door opening, or Victory UI panel) instead of instantly destroying the player or leaving them trapped in a locked room?',
    'Look at `StatManager.Die()`: if a player dies to your boss and `SceneManager.LoadScene(current.name)` reloads the arena, what happens to any coins or Double Jump unlock (`maxJumps`) stored on `StatManager`?',
  ],
};

const body = `
${renderAskBanner('how do I test a boss with friends and wire winning and dying?', 3)}

<p class="lead">
    First, finish the two endings: what happens when the boss reaches <code>0</code> HP, and
    clean verification when <code>StatManager.Die()</code> triggers. Then swap seats and let
    friends playtest your entire boss fight cold — zero coaching allowed while they play.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
${renderDecompose('8.5', DECOMPOSE, 3)}

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">In the Code + Editor: Wire Win &amp; Lose Cleanly (~20 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <table>
        <tr><th>Outcome</th><th>What Must Happen</th><th>How Your Project Already Supports It</th></tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Player Dies</strong></td>
            <td>Player restarts outside or at the boss room start with full HP and all hazards reset.</td>
            <td><code>StatManager.Die()</code> restores <code>health = maxHealth</code>, halves <code>coins</code>, and calls <code>SceneManager.LoadScene(current.name)</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Boss Dies</strong></td>
            <td>Boss stops firing, clears active hazards cleanly, and reveals an exit, treasure drop, or Victory screen.</td>
            <td><code>EnemyController.Die()</code> spawns <code>itemDrop</code> (e.g. trophy, portal, <code>SceneSwitch</code>, or Victory Canvas trigger) before calling <code>Destroy(gameObject)</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Replay</strong></td>
            <td>Player can play again (returning to <code>Start (index 0)</code> or re-entering <code>Overworld</code>) without restarting Unity.</td>
            <td><code>SceneSwitch</code> or a Play Again button calling <code>SceneManager.LoadScene(0)</code> resets cleanly while keeping one <code>StatManager</code>.</td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Closing Both Ends of the Fight</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>If your boss uses child <code>Turret</code> objects attached to the wall rather than children of the boss GameObject, destroying the boss leaves wall turrets still shooting during Victory! How do you turn them off cleanly in <code>Die()</code>?</li>
            <li>Suppose a player dies during your boss fight with <code>coins = 5</code>. After <code>StatManager.Die()</code> runs, what value does <code>coinText</code> display — and does <code>StatManager.Die()</code> currently update <code>coinText.text</code> inside <code>Die()</code> or only <code>healthText.text</code>?</li>
            <li>Where does a <code>SceneSwitch</code> (or Victory UI) go after the boss dies so a tester knows the game is beaten without asking you?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Studio: Blind Friend Playtesting (~40 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~40 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        Have <strong>two friends</strong> play your build back-to-back while you sit beside them
        with a notebook. Follow the strict silence rule:
    </p>

    <ol>
        <li><strong>Hands off &amp; mouth closed:</strong> start from <code>Start (index 0)</code> or your cave checkpoint and tell them only the keys if nothing on screen explains them — then say NOTHING for the next 3 minutes.</li>
        <li><strong>Record observations, not excuses:</strong> never say "oh yeah, ignore that bug" or "you were supposed to jump there." Write down the exact frame or spot where they got stuck, died unfairly, or missed how to hurt the boss.</li>
        <li><strong>Ask three questions after they finish (or die 3 times):</strong> (a) When did you know you were hurting the boss? (b) Which attack felt unfair or invisible? (c) Did you understand what happened when you won or died?</li>
    </ol>

    <table>
        <tr><th>Tester</th><th>Where They Hesitated</th><th>Bugs / Soft-Locks Seen</th><th>Quote From Tester</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Friend 1</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Friend 2</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>
    </table>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Turning Playtest Notes Into Revisions</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Name one thing BOTH testers struggled with that surprised you — why did it feel obvious to you while building, and what changed when someone saw it cold?</li>
            <li>Look at your notes and sort every item into three buckets: <strong>Confusion</strong> (did not know what to do), <strong>Bug</strong> (broken collider/null error/soft-lock), or <strong>Balance</strong> (too easy / too fast). Which bucket breaks the game fastest?</li>
            <li>What if a friend suggested adding a whole new second boss — why do good developers prioritize clarity and fairness fixes on what exists rather than starting from scratch right before deadline?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Verifying the Reset Loop</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>During friend playtesting, what happened on try #2 after your tester died to the boss — did everything reset cleanly cleanly without stuck triggers or double HUDs?</li>
            <li>Did your friend reach the Victory outcome on their own, or only after asking you where the exit/goal was?</li>
            <li>Pick the TOP TWO concrete revisions you will execute next class before Freeze &amp; Showcase.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="checklist">
    <h3>Checkpoint — before moving on, you must be able to:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Complete both victory (reward/portal/screen on boss defeat) and loss (<code>StatManager.Die()</code> clean reset)</li>
        <li>Observe two friends playtesting your boss cold without coaching them</li>
        <li>Categorize playtest notes into Confusion, Bugs, and Balance and pick top revisions</li>
        <li>Commit and push</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <p>Need a deeper explanation? These pages cover the same concepts:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-08/index.html">Unit 8: Boss Fight</a> — friend playtest protocol</li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-05/index.html">Unit 5: Persistence &amp; HUD</a> — <code>StatManager.Die()</code> scene reload flow</li>
        <li><a href="../docs/ask.html">How do I&hellip;? index</a> — find this lesson again by the question you were asking</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Next: <a href="8.6.html">8.6 — Boss Revisions &amp; Pre-Break Showcase</a> — apply your playtest fixes and ship cleanly before Winter Break.</p>
</div>`;
